`251-251`: **Batch counter starts at 1; off-by-one in final “batches” log**

Initialize batchCount to 0 and increment strictly on each executeBulkRequest to report accurate batch counts.


```diff
-            int batchCount = 1;
+            int batchCount = 0;
```

---

`265-272`: **Avoid materializing large content strings just to test “blank”**

If EntityContentProducer now exposes getContentSize(reference), prefer that first and only fall back to getContent(reference) when the size is unknown (<0). This reduces allocations and duplicate content fetches.


```diff
-                    // First check if document should be indexed (skip content checks early)
-                    if (StringUtils.isBlank(ecp.getContent(reference))) {
-                        continue;
-                    }
-                    
-                    // Only get document size when we intend to add the doc to the bulk
-                    long docSize = getDocumentSize(reference, ecp);
+                    // Prefer cheap size check; fall back to content read only if size is unknown
+                    long contentSize = ecp.getContentSize(reference);
+                    if (contentSize == 0) {
+                        continue;
+                    }
+                    if (contentSize < 0 && StringUtils.isBlank(ecp.getContent(reference))) {
+                        continue;
+                    }
+
+                    // Only get document size when we intend to add the doc to the bulk
+                    long docSize = getDocumentSize(reference, ecp);
```

---

`273-283`: **Tighten flush condition; avoid re-initializing a fresh BulkRequest when empty**

As written, the outer if triggers for an oversized single doc even when the bulk is empty, leading to a redundant new BulkRequest allocation. Tighten the condition to flush only when there are existing actions and the size limit would be exceeded; still flush on doc-count limit. This preserves the “one big doc is its own batch” behavior without empty re-inits.


```diff
-                    // Check batch limits and execute if needed
-                    if (bulkRequest.numberOfActions() >= bulkRequestSize || 
-                        currentBatchSizeBytes + docSize > contentIndexBatchMaxSizeBytes) {
-                        // Only flush if there are actions to execute
-                        if (bulkRequest.numberOfActions() > 0) {
-                            executeBulkRequest(bulkRequest);
-                            batchCount++;
-                        }
-                        bulkRequest = new BulkRequest();
-                        currentBatchSizeBytes = 0;
-                    }
+                    // Check batch limits and execute if needed (avoid empty flushes/re-inits)
+                    if (bulkRequest.numberOfActions() >= bulkRequestSize ||
+                        (bulkRequest.numberOfActions() > 0 &&
+                         currentBatchSizeBytes + docSize > contentIndexBatchMaxSizeBytes)) {
+                        executeBulkRequest(bulkRequest);
+                        batchCount++;
+                        bulkRequest = new BulkRequest();
+                        currentBatchSizeBytes = 0;
+                    }
```

