`619-619`: **Plain filenames in Content-Disposition fix the bug; consider RFC 5987 filename* + minimal sanitization for broader UA compatibility.**

Your change removes URL-encoding and lets parentheses and apostrophes display correctly in the download dialog — that addresses SAK-51813 directly. To harden this across browsers and locales (and avoid header injection via CR/LF or quotes), consider emitting both filename="..." and filename*=UTF-8''... while sanitizing control characters.


Apply this diff in each export method (XLS/CSV/PDF):

```diff
-        response.setAttachmentHeader(fileName + ".xls");
+        setContentDisposition(response, fileName + ".xls");
```

```diff
-        response.setAttachmentHeader(fileName + ".csv");
+        setContentDisposition(response, fileName + ".csv");
```

```diff
-        response.setAttachmentHeader(fileName + ".pdf");
+        setContentDisposition(response, fileName + ".pdf");
```

Add this helper (outside the shown ranges):

```java
// Add near other private helpers in this class
private static void setContentDisposition(WebResponse response, String filename) {
    // Strip CR/LF and double quotes to prevent header injection/breakage
    String safeAscii = filename.replace("\r", "_").replace("\n", "_").replace("\"", "'");
    String encoded = java.net.URLEncoder.encode(filename, java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets.UTF_8)
            .replace("+", "%20");
    // RFC 6266/5987: send both filename (ASCII, quoted) and filename* (UTF-8)
    response.setHeader("Content-Disposition",
            "attachment; filename=\"" + safeAscii + "\"; filename*=UTF-8''" + encoded);
}
```

Also remember to import:
```java
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.net.URLEncoder;
```


Please sanity-check downloads in Chrome, Firefox, Edge, and Safari with filenames containing: parentheses, apostrophes, comma, and a few non-ASCII chars (e.g., “é, 中文”). Verify the save dialog shows the exact name. If you prefer, I can provide a WicketTester-based test to assert the Content-Disposition header.


