`2211-2217`: **Broaden stringToDate to also accept date-only inputs**  

The `stringToDate` method currently only parses ISO datetimes with `inputDateTimeFormatter`. However, callers like `compareDates` may pass date-only strings (e.g. “2025-08-25”). Since `inputDateFormatter` already supports date-only patterns—including `"yyyy-MM-dd"`—we can gracefully fall back to it in the catch block rather than immediately erroring.  

• Location:  
  - File:  
    `site-manage/datemanager/impl/src/main/java/org/sakaiproject/datemanager/impl/DateManagerServiceImpl.java`  
  - Method: `stringToDate` (around lines 2211–2217)  

• Change (optional refactor):  
```diff
         try {
             LocalDateTime localDateTime = LocalDateTime.parse(dateString, inputDateTimeFormatter);
             return Date.from(localDateTime.atZone(zone).toInstant());
-        } catch (DateTimeParseException e) {
-            log.error("Failed to parse date string '{}' with format 'yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm:ss[+HH:MM]': {}", dateString, e.getMessage());
-            throw e;
+        } catch (DateTimeParseException e) {
+            // Fallback: parse as date-only (no time) using inputDateFormatter
+            try {
+                LocalDate dateOnly = LocalDate.parse(dateString, inputDateFormatter);
+                return Date.from(dateOnly.atStartOfDay(zone).toInstant());
+            } catch (DateTimeParseException ignored) {
+                log.warn("Unable to parse '{}' with either datetime or date-only formats", dateString, e);
+                throw e;
+            }
         }
```  

We’ve confirmed:  
- `inputDateFormatter` supports `"yyyy-MM-dd"` among other date-only patterns.  
- `DateManagerConstants.DATEPICKER_DATETIME_FORMAT` remains `"yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm:ss"`.  

This preserves existing behavior for full datetimes while avoiding false positives when only a date is provided.

