`2425-2434`: **Re-evaluate “same-hash replacement → new path” behavior.**

Forcing a new path when the replacement content’s hash equals the current file’s hash defeats dedup and creates duplicate blobs. With the pre-write hash and “reuse when duplicate” logic, self-overwrite cannot occur. Recommend reusing oldFilePath when duplicateFilePath.equals(oldFilePath).


Would you like a patch that simplifies this branch to prefer reuse for true no-op replacements?

---

`2409-2411`: **Zero-byte uploads: consider skipping FILE_PATH assignment and physical write.**

For 0-byte content, we typically don’t persist a physical file or set FILE_PATH. Current logic will set length/sha and may assign a new path. Guard and short-circuit to keep m_filePath null for zero-length.


```diff
- long byteCount = buffer.length;
+ long byteCount = buffer.length;
+ if (byteCount == 0) {
+   resource.setContentLength(0L);
+   resource.setContentSha256(StorageUtils.bytesToHex(MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256").digest(new byte[0])));
+   return true; // no FILE_PATH
+ }
```

</blockquote></details>
