And perform post-commit cleanup right after m_resourceStore.commitResource(edit) in commitResource(...):

```java
// Post-commit FS cleanup (safe after DB row persisted)
try {
    String oldPath = oldFilePathToDelete.get();
    if (oldPath != null && bodyPath != null) {
        boolean single = serverConfigurationService.getBoolean(PROP_SINGLE_INSTANCE, PROP_SINGLE_INSTANCE_DEFAULT);
        int refs = single ? countTotalFileReferences(oldPath) : 0;
        if (!single || refs == 0) {
            BaseResourceEdit tmp = new BaseResourceEdit(edit.getId());
            tmp.m_filePath = oldPath;
            delResourceBodyFilesystem(bodyPath, tmp);
            log.debug("Post-commit cleanup deleted old file path: {}", oldPath);
        } else {
            log.debug("Post-commit cleanup retained old file path {} with {} reference(s)", oldPath, refs);
        }
    }
} catch (Exception e) {
    log.warn("Post-commit cleanup skipped: {}", e.toString());
} finally {
    oldFilePathToDelete.remove();
}
```

