+                    Thread t = new Thread(r, "sakai-msg-" + System.nanoTime());
+                    t.setDaemon(true);
+                    t.setUncaughtExceptionHandler((th, ex) ->
+                        log.error("Uncaught exception in {}", th.getName(), ex));
+                    return t;
+                };
+                executor = new ThreadPoolExecutor(
+                        threadPoolSize, threadPoolSize,
+                        0L, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS,
+                        new LinkedBlockingQueue<>(queueCapacity),
+                        tf,
+                        new ThreadPoolExecutor.CallerRunsPolicy()  // preserves sync fallback
+                );
+                log.info("Initialized messaging thread pool with {} threads and queue capacity {}", threadPoolSize, queueCapacity);
```

---

`226-235`: **Harden submitNotificationTask to surface uncaught exceptions.**

Wrap tasks so unexpected RuntimeExceptions are logged uniformly; optionally use submit(...) instead of execute(...) to allow callers to get Futures when needed.



```diff
     public void submitNotificationTask(Runnable task) {
         Objects.requireNonNull(task, "task");
         if (executor != null) {
-            executor.execute(task);
+            executor.execute(withErrorBoundary(task));
         } else {
-            task.run();
+            withErrorBoundary(task).run();
         }
     }
+
+    private Runnable withErrorBoundary(Runnable task) {
+        return () -> {
+            try {
+                task.run();
+            } catch (Throwable t) {
+                log.error("Unhandled exception in notification task", t);
+            }
+        };
+    }
```

---

`615-618`: **Fix misleading log message on push send failures.**

The catch covers both serialization and HTTP send errors, but the log says “serialize”. Log the endpoint and exception, and attach the throwable to error.



```diff
-            } catch (Exception e) {
-                log.error("Failed to serialize notification for push: {}", e.toString());
-                log.debug("Stacktrace", e);
-            }
+            } catch (Exception e) {
+                log.error("Failed to send push notification to {}: {}", pushEndpoint, e.getMessage(), e);
+            }
```

---

`606-614`: **Consider handling transient push responses with retry/backoff.**

429/5xx should not delete subscriptions; add retry/backoff (or enqueue) and only purge on 410/404/400 as you already do.

