`159-163`: **Centralize suffix-trim; prefer class constant and avoid mutating getter**

getText() already returns DEFAULT_FORMULA when formula == null (no NPE risk), but still extract the suffix logic and use a class constant rather than a per-iteration local; avoid mutating getters where possible.

```diff
-                final String SUFFIX = "|0,0";
-                String text = globalvariable.getText();
-                if (text.endsWith(SUFFIX)) {
-                    globalvariable.setText(text.substring(0, text.length() - SUFFIX.length()));
-                }
+                globalvariable.setText(stripSuffixIfPresent(globalvariable.getText()));
```

Add to the class:

```java
private static final String TEXT_SUFFIX = "|0,0";

private static String stripSuffixIfPresent(String text) {
    if (text == null) return null;
    return text.endsWith(TEXT_SUFFIX)
        ? text.substring(0, text.length() - TEXT_SUFFIX.length())
        : text;
}
```

Optional: keep getters side‑effect free — call stripSuffixIfPresent for presentation and move mutation to addGlobalVariable(...) or bean construction.

