> `668-703`: **Add connection/read timeouts and use HTTP HEAD in CPValidator’s external URL checks**
> 
> CPValidator.validate(...) is invoked synchronously in ScormContentServiceImpl during content‐package import, so unbounded GET requests can block request threads without limits. In `scormplayer/scorm-impl/adl/src/java/org/adl/validator/contentpackage/CPValidator.java` (lines 668–703), change the URL check to use `HEAD`, set `connectTimeout`/`readTimeout`, and call `disconnect()` in `finally`:
> 
> ```diff
> -                try {
> -                    URL url = new URL(iURIString);
> -                    URLConnection urlConn = url.openConnection();
> -                    HttpURLConnection httpUrlConn = (HttpURLConnection) urlConn;
> -                    int code = httpUrlConn.getResponseCode();
> +                HttpURLConnection httpUrlConn = null;
> +                try {
> +                    httpUrlConn = (HttpURLConnection) new URL(iURIString).openConnection();
> +                    httpUrlConn.setRequestMethod("HEAD");
> +                    httpUrlConn.setInstanceFollowRedirects(true);
> +                    httpUrlConn.setConnectTimeout(5000);
> +                    httpUrlConn.setReadTimeout(5000);
> +                    int code = httpUrlConn.getResponseCode();
>                      if (code == 200) {
>                          msgText = Messages.getString("CPValidator.502", iURIString);
>                          log.debug("PASSED: {}", msgText);
>                      } else {
>                          msgText = Messages.getString("CPValidator.505", iURIString);
>                          log.debug("FAILED: {}", msgText);
>                          DetailedLogMessageCollection.getInstance()
>                              .addMessage(new LogMessage(MessageType.FAILED, msgText));
>                          result = false;
>                      }
> -                } catch (MalformedURLException mfue) {
