`82-90`: **Blocking: still using the removed JDBC-ODBC bridge**

Targeting Java 17 means `sun.jdbc.odbc.JdbcOdbcDriver` no longer exists; `Class.forName(...).newInstance()` will throw and we never obtain a connection. Please make the driver/URL configurable and fail fast with a clear error when they are absent or the class cannot be loaded, instead of defaulting to the legacy bridge.

```diff
-            String driverName = "sun.jdbc.odbc.JdbcOdbcDriver";
-            String connectionURL = "jdbc:odbc:SCORM3RDSSP10";
+            String driverName = System.getProperty("ssp.db.driver", System.getenv("SSP_DB_DRIVER"));
+            String connectionURL = System.getProperty("ssp.db.url", System.getenv("SSP_DB_URL"));
+            if (driverName == null || connectionURL == null) {
+                log.error("Database driver/URL not configured. Set ssp.db.driver and ssp.db.url or SSP_DB_DRIVER and SSP_DB_URL.");
+                return null;
+            }
@@
-            Class.forName(driverName).newInstance();
-            conn = DriverManager.getConnection(connectionURL, prop);
+            try {
+                Class.forName(driverName);
+            } catch (ClassNotFoundException cnfe) {
+                log.error("JDBC driver class not found: {}", driverName, cnfe);
+                return null;
+            }
+            conn = DriverManager.getConnection(connectionURL, prop);
```

As per coding guidelines.

