The get-then-remove sequence still allows a race where another thread can re-register a provider for the same prefix after line 48 but before line 52, causing the newly registered provider to be incorrectly removed.




Apply the previously suggested fix to use atomic compare-and-remove:

```diff
    public void unregisterProvider(String prefix, T provider) {
       if (prefix == null) {
          return;
       }
       WeakReference<T> current = prefixMap.get(prefix);
       if (current != null) {
          T existing = current.get();
          if (existing == null || existing == provider) {
-            prefixMap.remove(prefix);
+            prefixMap.remove(prefix, current);
          }
       }
    }
```

This ensures you only remove the exact `WeakReference` you checked, preventing accidental removal of a concurrently registered provider.

