`718-737`: **Consider filtering additional non-bean types.**

The current logic correctly filters most common non-bean types. However, several additional JDK types are typically leaf values not meant for bean introspection:

- I/O types: `java.io.File`, `java.nio.file.Path`
- Network types: `java.net.URI`, `java.net.URL`
- Identifier types: `java.util.UUID`
- i18n types: `java.util.Locale`, `java.util.Currency`
- Metadata: `Class<?>`

While these edge cases are less common, filtering them would prevent unnecessary reflection attempts.



Example expansion:

```diff
     if (Map.class.isAssignableFrom(type) || java.util.Collection.class.isAssignableFrom(type)) {
         return false;
     }
+    // Additional non-bean types
+    if (Class.class.equals(type) || java.util.UUID.class.equals(type)) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    String packageName = type.getPackage() != null ? type.getPackage().getName() : "";
+    if (packageName.startsWith("java.io.") || packageName.startsWith("java.nio.file.")
+            || packageName.startsWith("java.net.")) {
+        return false;
+    }
     return true;
```

