`377-390`: **Consider static initialization or double-checked locking for codec registry.**

The lazy initialization pattern has a check-then-act race condition. Multiple threads could simultaneously initialize separate codec registries. While the impact is minimal (identical registries), best practice is to use static initialization or double-checked locking with a volatile field.



Apply this diff to use static initialization:

```diff
-    private Map<String, EntityCodec> codecs;
-    private EntityCodec getCodec(String format) {
-        if (codecs == null) {
-            codecs = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
-            codecs.put(Formats.JSON, new JsonCodec());
-            codecs.put(Formats.XML, new XmlCodec());
-            codecs.put(Formats.HTML, new HtmlCodec());
-        }
+    private static final Map<String, EntityCodec> CODECS;
+    static {
+        Map<String, EntityCodec> map = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
+        map.put(Formats.JSON, new JsonCodec());
+        map.put(Formats.XML, new XmlCodec());
+        map.put(Formats.HTML, new HtmlCodec());
+        CODECS = map;
+    }
+    
+    private EntityCodec getCodec(String format) {
-        EntityCodec codec = codecs.get(format);
+        EntityCodec codec = CODECS.get(format);
         if (codec == null) {
             throw new IllegalArgumentException("Failed to find an encoder/decoder for format: " + format);
         }
         return codec;
     }
```

