<details>
<summary>entitybroker/impl/src/java/org/sakaiproject/entitybroker/impl/event/EventReceiverCoordinator.java (1)</summary><blockquote>

`49-90`: **Receivers keyed by ClassLoader still overwrite and leak**

Keying the `WeakHashMap` by `ClassLoader` means every bean from the same loader clobbers the previous one, so only one receiver survives. Worse, the strong reference to the `EventReceiver` instance keeps its `Class` (and thus `ClassLoader`) alive, so the weak key never clears and the entry sticks around indefinitely—no leak prevention at all. Please store the receivers themselves as the weak keys (e.g., `WeakHashMap<EventReceiver, Boolean>`) and snapshot the `keySet()` when dispatching, as previously suggested.

