When `userDirectoryService` is a JDK dynamic proxy (common for interface-based Spring beans), `target.getClass()` returns the proxy class (e.g., `$Proxy123`) instead of the implementation class containing `m_separateIdEid`. This causes `ReflectionUtils.findField(...)` to return `null`, forcing `usesSeparateIdEid` to `false` regardless of the actual field value—a regression from the previous `FieldUtils`-based approach which handled proxy unwrapping.



