<summary>kernel/kernel-impl/src/main/java/org/sakaiproject/tool/impl/RebuildBreakdownServiceImpl.java (1)</summary><blockquote>

`886-900`: **Critical: Guard against non-serializable types to prevent ClassCastException.**

The previous review comment on this code segment remains unaddressed. `isObjectSimple` returns `true` for any type assignable from interfaces in `SIMPLE_ASSIGNABLE_TYPES` (e.g., `CharSequence`, `TemporalAccessor`) without verifying that the concrete class implements `Serializable`. This will cause a `ClassCastException` at line 521 in `serializeSessionAttribute` when casting to `(Serializable) object` for types like `java.nio.CharBuffer`.




Apply this diff to add the Serializable check:

```diff
     private boolean isObjectSimple(Object object) {
         if (object == null) {
             return false;
         }
         Class<?> clazz = object.getClass();
         if (clazz.isPrimitive() || ClassUtils.isPrimitiveOrWrapper(clazz) || clazz.isEnum()) {
             return true;
         }
         for (Class<?> simpleType : SIMPLE_ASSIGNABLE_TYPES) {
-            if (simpleType.isAssignableFrom(clazz)) {
+            if (simpleType.isAssignableFrom(clazz) && Serializable.class.isAssignableFrom(clazz)) {
                 return true;
             }
         }
         return false;
     }
```

