`28-29`: **Catch `InaccessibleObjectException`/`SecurityException` when making members accessible**

On JDK 17+, `ReflectionUtils.makeAccessible(..)` delegates to `setAccessible(true)` and can raise `InaccessibleObjectException` or `SecurityException` for strongly encapsulated modules. Because we only catch `IllegalStateException`, those runtime failures now bubble up and turn the whole REST call into a 500 instead of falling back to the default timestamp. Please broaden the catch (same for both helpers) so we degrade gracefully.

```diff
-import java.lang.reflect.Field;
-import java.lang.reflect.Method;
+import java.lang.reflect.Field;
+import java.lang.reflect.InaccessibleObjectException;
+import java.lang.reflect.Method;
@@
-        } catch (IllegalStateException e) {
+        } catch (IllegalStateException | SecurityException | InaccessibleObjectException e) {
             return null;
         }
@@
-        } catch (IllegalStateException e) {
+        } catch (IllegalStateException | SecurityException | InaccessibleObjectException e) {
             return null;
         }
```

Based on learnings


Also applies to: 1214-1235

