<details>
<summary>kernel/kernel-impl/src/main/java/org/sakaiproject/content/impl/BaseContentService.java (1)</summary><blockquote>

`7737-7776`: **Re-use commitResource pipeline (virus scan/quota/events) instead of raw storage commit**

The new block bypasses `commitResource(...)` and talks directly to `m_storage.commitResource(edit)` while manually firing events. That short-circuits virus scanning, MIME detection, quota enforcement, availability scheduling, cache invalidation, etc., and the events now publish before we know the write succeeded (or will double-fire elsewhere). It also leaves the edit active if a failure bubbles up.

Please hand the edit to `commitResource(edit, NotificationService.NOTI_NONE)` and let the standard pipeline manage events/availability/quota/cleanup. On failure (e.g. quota/virus) cancel the edit so we don’t leak a half-written resource.

For example:

```diff
-                            // Register the events
-                            this.eventTrackingService.post(this.eventTrackingService.newEvent(EVENT_RESOURCE_ADD, edit.getReference(), true, NotificationService.NOTI_NONE));
-                            boolean contentUpdated = ((BaseResourceEdit) edit).m_body != null || ((BaseResourceEdit) edit).m_contentStream != null;
-                            if (contentUpdated){
-                                this.eventTrackingService.post(this.eventTrackingService.newEvent(EVENT_RESOURCE_UPD_NEW_VERSION, edit.getReference(), true, NotificationService.NOTI_NONE));
-                            }
-                            // complete the edit
-                            m_storage.commitResource(edit);
-                            ((BaseResourceEdit) edit).closeEdit();
+                            try {
+                                commitResource(edit, NotificationService.NOTI_NONE);
+                            } catch (OverQuotaException | ServerOverloadException | VirusFoundException e) {
+                                cancelResource(edit);
+                                throw e;
+                            }
```

