> 
> `46-87`: **Thread-safety issue: SimpleDateFormat is not thread-safe.**
> 
> The static `SimpleDateFormat` instance is shared across all threads and mutated by `applyPattern()` in each method. This creates a race condition where concurrent calls to `format_h_mm_a()`, `format_date_h_mm_a()`, or `format_date_mm_dd_yy()` can produce incorrect results or throw exceptions.
> 
> 
> 
> **Solution 1 (Recommended): Use thread-local SimpleDateFormat**
> 
> ```diff
> -	public static SimpleDateFormat dateFormat = new SimpleDateFormat();
> +	private static final ThreadLocal<SimpleDateFormat> dateFormat = ThreadLocal.withInitial(SimpleDateFormat::new);
>  
>  	public static String format_h_mm_a(Date date) {
>  		if (date == null)
>  			return "";
> -		dateFormat.applyPattern("h:mm a");
> -		return dateFormat.format(date);
> +		SimpleDateFormat formatter = dateFormat.get();
> +		formatter.applyPattern("h:mm a");
> +		return formatter.format(date);
>  	}
>  
>  	public static String format_date_h_mm_a(Date date) {
>  		if (date == null)
>  			return "";
> -		dateFormat.applyPattern("MM/dd/yy h:mm a");
> -		return dateFormat.format(date);
> +		SimpleDateFormat formatter = dateFormat.get();
> +		formatter.applyPattern("MM/dd/yy h:mm a");
> +		return formatter.format(date);
>  	}
>  
>  	public static String format_date_mm_dd_yy(Date date) {
>  		if (date == null)
>  			return "";
> -		dateFormat.applyPattern("MM/dd/yy");
> -		return dateFormat.format(date);
> +		SimpleDateFormat formatter = dateFormat.get();
> +		formatter.applyPattern("MM/dd/yy");
> +		return formatter.format(date);
>  	}
> ```
> 
> **Solution 2 (Modern Java): Use DateTimeFormatter (immutable and thread-safe)**
> 
> ```diff
> +import java.time.Instant;
> +import java.time.LocalDateTime;
> +import java.time.ZoneId;
> +import java.time.format.DateTimeFormatter;
> -import java.text.SimpleDateFormat;
>  import java.util.Date;
>  
