Use Objects.equals to avoid NPE if either side is null.


```diff
@@
+import java.util.Objects;
@@
-        return attendees == null ? null : attendees.stream()
-                .filter(attendee -> attendee.getAttendeeUserId().equals(attendeeId))
+        return attendees == null ? null : attendees.stream()
+                .filter(attendee -> Objects.equals(attendee.getAttendeeUserId(), attendeeId))
                 .findFirst()
                 .orElse(null);
@@
-        return waitingList == null ? null : waitingList.stream()
-                .filter(waiter -> waiter.getAttendeeUserId().equals(attendeeId))
+        return waitingList == null ? null : waitingList.stream()
+                .filter(waiter -> Objects.equals(waiter.getAttendeeUserId(), attendeeId))
                 .findFirst()
                 .orElse(null);
```


Also applies to: 151-156, 166-171

