---

`647-719`: **Consider extracting common metadata processing logic.**

The objectives and keywords sections share nearly identical patterns:
- Split comma-separated values
- Trim and filter empty entries  
- Parse percentage values defensively
- Calculate running averages

Extracting this into a helper method would reduce duplication and ensure consistent handling.



Example structure:

```java
private void processMetadataTag(String metadataValue, 
                                 HistogramQuestionScoresBean questionScores,
                                 Map<String, Double> correctMap,
                                 Map<String, Integer> counterMap) {
    if (metadataValue == null || metadataValue.isEmpty()) {
        return;
    }

    String[] entries = metadataValue.split(",");
    for (String entry : entries) {
        entry = entry.trim();
        if (entry.isEmpty()) {
            continue;
        }

        Double pctCorrect = parsePercentCorrect(questionScores);
        updateAverages(entry, pctCorrect, correctMap, counterMap);
    }
}
```

Then call with:
```java
processMetadataTag(questionScores.getObjectives(), questionScores, objectivesCorrect, objectivesCounter);
processMetadataTag(questionScores.getKeywords(), questionScores, keywordsCorrect, keywordsCounter);
```

