`61-86`: **Consider reusing a shared `XmlMapper` instead of constructing per‑call**

Both `parseRequest` and `parseResponse` create and configure a new `XmlMapper` on every invocation. For a servlet‑style environment this adds unnecessary object churn; using a single, statically configured `XmlMapper` (similar to `ServiceServlet.POX_XML_MAPPER`) would be cheaper and still thread‑safe once configuration is complete.

If you align the configuration with the rest of the POX stack (e.g., `FAIL_ON_UNKNOWN_PROPERTIES=false`, `setDefaultUseWrapper(false)`), you can centralize it in a static field and reuse it across all parse methods.



