```

This:
- Truncates any fractional percentage via cast to `int`, and
- Only asserts that the setter/getter work, not that the service computes percentages as expected.



Consider revising to:
- Assert directly on what the service returns (e.g., via `getGradeDefinitionForStudentForItem` or a dedicated percentage-accessor), and
- Preserve decimals or round explicitly, e.g.:

```diff
- gradeDef.setGrade(String.valueOf((int) percentage));
- assertEquals("50", gradeDef.getGrade());
+ gradeDef.setGrade(String.format(Locale.ROOT, "%.2f", percentage));
+ assertEquals("50.00", gradeDef.getGrade());
```

or update the expectation to match the actual service behavior. Please align the test with the production rounding rules used for percentage entry.

