`195-211`: **SHA-1 usage is spec-mandated for OAuth 1.0a body hash.**

The static analysis flagged SHA-1 as insecure, but this is required by the OAuth 1.0a specification for `oauth_body_hash` computation. The code correctly supports SHA-256 when `HMAC-SHA256` signature method is used (lines 197-199).

However, `postBody.getBytes()` on line 200 uses the platform default charset, which may cause hash mismatches if the client and server use different encodings. The OAuth spec recommends UTF-8.


<details>
<summary>🔎 Proposed fix to specify UTF-8 charset</summary>

```diff
-            md.update(postBody.getBytes());
+            md.update(postBody.getBytes(java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
```
</details>

