`34-38`: **Consider configuring daemon threads for the executor.**

The thread pool threads are not explicitly configured as daemon threads. Non-daemon threads can prevent JVM shutdown if tasks are still running.



<details>
<summary>💡 Use a custom ThreadFactory to create daemon threads</summary>

```diff
 public void init() {

     int poolSize = serverConfigurationService.getInt("schedulingservice.poolsize", 4);
-    executor = Executors.newScheduledThreadPool(poolSize);
+    executor = Executors.newScheduledThreadPool(poolSize, r -> {
+        Thread t = new Thread(r);
+        t.setDaemon(true);
+        t.setName("SchedulingService-" + t.getId());
+        return t;
+    });
 }
```
</details>

---

`40-43`: **Consider graceful shutdown instead of abrupt termination.**

`shutdownNow()` immediately stops all executing tasks and may leave work incomplete. Consider a graceful shutdown approach that allows tasks to complete.



<details>
<summary>💡 Implement graceful shutdown</summary>

```diff
 public void destroy() {

-    executor.shutdownNow();
+    executor.shutdown();
+    try {
+        if (!executor.awaitTermination(30, TimeUnit.SECONDS)) {
+            executor.shutdownNow();
+            if (!executor.awaitTermination(10, TimeUnit.SECONDS)) {
+                log.warn("Executor did not terminate");
+            }
+        }
+    } catch (InterruptedException ie) {
+        executor.shutdownNow();
+        Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
+    }
 }
```

This gives tasks 30 seconds to complete normally before forcing shutdown.
</details>

---

