> <summary>webcomponents/tool/src/main/frontend/packages/sakai-notifications/src/SakaiNotifications.js (1)</summary><blockquote>
> 
> `87-90`: **Restore `credentials: "include"` to the initial notifications fetch.**
> 
> The `/users/me/notifications` endpoint requires authentication via `checkSakaiSession()`. Removing `credentials: "include"` prevents the browser from sending authentication cookies, causing the initial notification load to fail with a 403 Forbidden response.
> 
> <details>
> <summary>🔧 Required fix</summary>
> 
> ```diff
>  fetch(this.url, {
>    cache: "no-cache",
>    headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
> +  credentials: "include",
>  })
> ```
> </details>
> 
> </blockquote></details>
> <details>
> <summary>samigo/samigo-app/src/java/org/sakaiproject/tool/assessment/ui/queue/delivery/TimedAssessmentQueue.java (1)</summary><blockquote>
> 
> `31-81`: **Fix thread-safety, null-safety, and logging issues in task scheduling and removal.**
> 
> 1. **NPE in remove()**: Line 94 calls `tasks.get(timedAG).cancel(true)` without null check; if the task doesn't exist, this crashes.
> 2. **Unsafe task map**: Line 44 uses `HashMap<Long, ScheduledFuture<?>>` which is not thread-safe; must be `ConcurrentHashMap`.
> 3. **Unchecked null SchedulingService**: Line 47 passes `ComponentManager.get(SchedulingService.class)` to constructor without null check; if unavailable, calling `schedulingService.scheduleAtFixedRate()` at line 72 will NPE.
> 4. **Queue entry left on scheduling failure**: Line 66 adds to queue before scheduling (line 71–76); if scheduling throws (line 78), the queue entry remains with no corresponding task.
