<details>
<summary>kernel/kernel-impl/src/main/java/org/sakaiproject/messaging/impl/UserMessagingServiceImpl.java (2)</summary><blockquote>

`573-604`: **Optimize broadcast push for large user bases.**

The current implementation pages through all users and calls `decorateNotification` for each one, which performs database lookups for user details and site information. For systems with thousands of users, this could cause performance issues and database load spikes.

Consider optimizing by:
- Batch-fetching user display names before the loop
- Avoiding decoration for push notifications (push client can decorate on receipt)
- Using a background job queue for very large broadcasts



<details>
<summary>💡 Alternative approach sketch</summary>

```java
private void pushToAllUsers(UserNotificationTransferBean bean) {
    executor.execute(() -> {
        int pageSize = 100;
        int first = 1;
        int total = userDirectoryService.countUsers();

        // Prepare the base notification once
        UserNotificationTransferBean un = new UserNotificationTransferBean();
        un.from = bean.from;
        un.event = bean.event;
        un.ref = bean.ref;
        un.title = bean.title;
        // Avoid calling decorateNotification per user

        while (first < total) {
            int last = first + pageSize;
            List<User> users = userDirectoryService.getUsers(first, last);

            // Push without decoration; client decorates
            users.forEach(u -> {
                un.to = u.getId();
                push(un); // Push without decoration
            });

            first = last + 1;
        }
    });
}
```

Note: This assumes push clients can handle undecorated notifications.
</details>

