`70-71`: The URL field in UserNotification has not had a breaking schema change. The field was already optional (without explicit `nullable = false`) and remains optional. No constraint removal occurred.

Looking at the git history, the URL field at line 70 shows `[user](name="URL", length = 2048)` in both the current code and prior versions—it was never explicitly marked as `nullable = false`. This is intentional design: optional fields like URL, TITLE, SITE_ID, VIEWED, and END_DATE contrast with required fields like ID, FROM_USER, TO_USER, EVENT, REF, EVENT_DATE, and DEFERRED, which explicitly specify `nullable = false`.

The commit SAK-51956 ("Add broadcast type notification") logically supports optional URLs, as broadcast notifications may not require a specific URL destination.

No database migration is needed because the schema constraint was not changed.



